---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ | Bush Gums"
  description="Answers about Bush Gums product research, affiliate links, kits and comparisons."
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h1>Good questions before a first overnight.</h1>
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>Does Bush Gums sell these products?</summary><p>
            No. Bush Gums curates research and links to external merchant
            listings. We do not own inventory, take payment or fulfil orders.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do affiliate links work?</summary><p>
            Some merchant links are affiliate links. If you buy through one,
            Bush Gums may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. The
            affiliate relationship does not turn a seller claim into independent
            evidence. Read the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/"
              >affiliate disclosure</a
            >.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are prices live?</summary><p>
            No. Prices on research pages are what Bush Gums paid or recorded.
            External merchant prices, stock, shipping and terms can change.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Have you tested these products yourselves?</summary><p>
            No. Our picks are based on owner experiences, independent reviews,
            forums and videos. Each product page shows the evidence and sources
            behind the pick. See <a href="/about/#how-we-choose"
              >how we choose gear</a
            >.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What do seller claim and to verify mean?</summary><p>
            Seller claim means a figure comes from a listing or seller and has
            not been independently confirmed. To verify means we do not yet have
            reliable evidence for the figure.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are the current kits appropriate for winter?</summary><p>
            No. We do not currently recommend either Bush Gums kit for winter
            conditions. Winter trips require route-specific decisions about
            shelter, sleeping-bag warmth, ground insulation, weather exposure
            and safety margins. Our <a
              href="/guides/sleeping-bag-temperature-ratings/"
              >sleeping bag guide</a
            >
            explains one part of that decision.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is not included in the core kit?</summary><p>
            The core totals cover shelter, sleep and pack items only. Clothing,
            navigation, food, water, first aid, communications and trip-specific
            safety gear need separate planning. Cooking and comfort items are
            optional add-ons. Use the <a
              href="/guides/overnight-hike-packing-list/"
              >overnight packing list</a
            >
            to plan the rest.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How is the Anaconda comparison constructed?</summary><p>
            It is a dated, category-matched comparison rather than a claim that
            the products are identical. Delivery is excluded. Bush Gums figures
            are recorded prices, while Anaconda figures use advertised sale or
            Club prices, listed weights and retained comparison estimates.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why can listed weights differ?</summary><p>
            Sources may describe a technical minimum, a packed weight or a
            carried estimate, and accessories may be included or excluded. We
            label the evidence basis and do not treat a missing weight as zero.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if an external merchant changes the listing?</summary><p
          >
            Merchant listings can change or disappear. Check the current
            listing, specifications, price, shipping, returns and warranty
            before purchasing, and contact the merchant about the transaction.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
